==============================================================================
WARNINGS ON THE INVENTORY ITSELF
==============================================================================

  1. THIS DOCKERFILE IS BYTE-IDENTICAL TO runtime/go/v1.25/Dockerfile
     runtime/go/v1.25 and runtime/go/v1.26 carry the same Dockerfile, the same
     bin/compile and the same lib/launcher.go, and both build FROM
     golang:1.26-bookworm with
     OW_EXECUTION_ENV=apacheopenserverless/runtime-golang-v1.26.
     The two directories therefore publish the same contents under two
     different tags, and the bundled-software inventory recorded here is the
     same for both. The v1.25 directory is the one that is wrong: either its
     FROM line must go back to golang:1.25-bookworm, or the directory and its
     tag must be retired. Until that is resolved, the Go toolchain version
     named in the v1.25 LICENSE and NOTICE cannot be reconciled with the
     release coordinates of that image.

  2. FLOATING BASE IMAGE AND apt-get upgrade
     The base image is referenced by tag, not by digest, and the Dockerfile
     runs `apt-get update && apt-get upgrade -y`. The exact set of bundled
     operating-system packages therefore changes between builds of the same
     source tree. This inventory describes the components the Dockerfile
     names; it cannot be exact for every build.

  3. TRANSITIVE DEBIAN DEPENDENCIES ARE NOT ENUMERATED
     `apt-get install curl jq zip librdkafka1 librdkafka++1 librdkafka-dev`
     pulls further Debian packages that are installed into the image and are
     not listed in LICENSE or NOTICE -- among them the TLS, SASL and
     compression libraries that librdkafka and curl link against, and the
     regular-expression library that jq links against. Their copyright files
     are in /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright inside the image. They are
     part of the convenience binary, not of the source release; a complete
     per-package inventory can only be produced from a built image.

  4. LICENSE TEXTS WERE TAKEN FROM UPSTREAM, NOT FROM A BUILT IMAGE
     The texts concatenated into LICENSE come from the upstream projects, at
     the module versions recorded in go.mod for the Go dependencies and from
     the upstream source for the Debian packages. Debian may ship a different
     revision of the same license text, and the authoritative copy for the
     shipped binaries remains /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright inside the
     image.

  5. THE BUNDLED PROXY CANNOT BE VERIFIED FROM THIS DIRECTORY
     /bin/proxy is copied from the image named by the COMMON build argument,
     which defaults to `missing:missing`. The Go module inventory in LICENSE
     and NOTICE was derived from the go.mod and go.sum of this repository. If
     the image passed as COMMON is built from a different source tree, the
     modules actually linked into /bin/proxy may differ.

  6. librdkafka-dev IS A DEVELOPMENT PACKAGE
     Headers and the static library are installed into a runtime image. They
     are not needed to run actions and they enlarge the set of third-party
     material shipped in the convenience binary.

  7. DEPENDENCIES OF USER ACTIONS ARE NOT COVERED
     This image ships no preinstalled Go libraries: user actions declare
     their own dependencies, which /bin/compile fetches at action-compile
     time. Those libraries are NOT part of this image and NOT part of any
     Apache release artifact, and no claim is made here about their licenses.


